---
# Bootloader clang-tidy config.
#
# Scope: the CI gate (`.github/workflows/build-and-test.yml` → `clang-tidy`
# job) runs clang-tidy-diff so warnings only fail the build on lines this
# PR actually touched. That means we can land this config without first
# doing a big-bang cleanup of the existing tree — tightening checks costs
# nothing on untouched code, and PRs are nudged toward the rules going
# forward.
#
# Why each family is on:
#   bugprone-*           correctness — bugprone-unused-return-value would
#                        have caught the discarded HAL_FDCAN_AddMessageTo-
#                        TxFifoQ return that drove Bug B in issue #94.
#   readability-*        naming / brace / declaration style.
#   cert-*               CERT C secure-coding rules.
#   clang-analyzer-*     null-deref / leaks / use-after-free.
#   misc-*               misc gotchas (unused-using-decls etc.).
#
# Carve-outs — never disable a check without writing the why next to it:
#   readability-magic-numbers       Embedded register constants are
#                                   intentionally inline; pulling each
#                                   one into a named #define hurts
#                                   readability more than it helps.
#   readability-isolate-declaration Stylistic; codebase already keeps
#                                   declarations short by convention.
#   readability-identifier-length   ARM HAL APIs use short names (msp,
#                                   id, n); the rule's 1–3-char minimum
#                                   is too aggressive for this codebase.
#   readability-braces-around-statements
#                                   The codebase uses K&R single-line
#                                   ifs intentionally for guard clauses;
#                                   forcing braces hurts diff churn.
#   bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters
#                                   Heuristic that flags any two adjacent
#                                   same-type params — far too noisy.
#   bugprone-reserved-identifier    STM32 HAL macros use `_foo` style and
#                                   trip this check via transitive headers.
#   bugprone-macro-parentheses      Most BL macros are simple value
#                                   constants where the parens harm
#                                   readability. Selective fix in code,
#                                   not a global gate.
#   cert-err34-c                    We use atoi-style parsing in the
#                                   serial-cli command handlers
#                                   deliberately; the inputs are
#                                   developer-typed, not untrusted.
#   cert-dcl16-c                    L/U suffix on every integer literal
#                                   is pedantic for this codebase.
#   misc-no-recursion               Occasional recursion in test
#                                   helpers (mock_flash, nvm sim).
#   misc-include-cleaner            Noisy on STM32 HAL transitive
#                                   headers; needs a separate cleanup PR.
#
# HeaderFilterRegex: only emit diagnostics for headers inside Core/Inc/bl_*.
# Without this, transitively-included HAL / CMSIS headers would generate
# thousands of warnings irrelevant to our changes.
Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  readability-*,
  cert-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  misc-*,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -readability-isolate-declaration,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -readability-braces-around-statements,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-reserved-identifier,
  -bugprone-macro-parentheses,
  -cert-err34-c,
  -cert-dcl16-c,
  -misc-no-recursion,
  -misc-include-cleaner
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: 'Core/Inc/bl_.*'
FormatStyle: none
